From: Null IDE <build@nullide>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: inject null CSS and splash screen into workbench.html

Adds a stylesheet link for null-custom.css (workbench overrides) and a
script tag for null-splash.js (branded loading screen). Both files are
copied into the workbench/browser directory by build.sh before the gulp
build runs, so this patch never needs to change between VS Code versions.
---
 src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html b/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
--- a/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/browser/workbench.html
@@ -1,7 +1,9 @@
 <!DOCTYPE html>
 <html>
 	<head>
 		<meta charset="utf-8" />
 		<link rel="stylesheet" data-name="vs/workbench/workbench.desktop.main" href="workbench.desktop.main.css">
+		<link rel="stylesheet" href="null-custom.css">
+		<script src="null-splash.js"></script>
 	</head>
 	<body aria-label=""></body>
 </html>
